{"id": "wd-Q131341151", "status": "ok", "meta": "Viktor Vasnetsov's 1914 painting The Guard, a repeat of an earlier work, in the Donetsk Regional Museum of Art.", "about": "A bearded warrior in a conical helmet and blue tunic carries a long-bladed axe on his shoulder and a round metal shield at his side. Behind him are golden onion domes and a church cross above a brick wall. Viktor Vasnetsov painted this small version on canvas glued to plywood. It repeats a picture of the same name that went to a private collection in New York in 1924 and came up at Christie's in November 2013.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuard_by_V.Vasnetsov_(1914%2C_Donetsk_museum).jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuard_by_V.Vasnetsov_(1914%2C_Donetsk_museum).jpg"], "check": "clean"}
